# Shared Component Architecture

Mirror the page pattern: each reusable feature gets its own directory under `src/components/shared/` with `components/` and `container/` when logic is needed.

## Directory Structure

```
src/components/shared/{feature}/
  index.ts                  # Public API — export container as default entry when applicable
  {feature}.utils.ts        # Constants, config maps, pure helpers (no JSX)
  components/
    index.ts
    {SubPiece}.tsx          # Small presentational pieces (CountryFlag, CountryDialCode)
    {Feature}.tsx           # Pure UI — props in, JSX out
  container/
    index.ts
    {Feature}Container.tsx  # Sanitization, defaults, wiring — only when needed
```

## Responsibilities

| Layer | Owns | Must NOT own |
|-------|------|--------------|
| **Component** | Layout, styling, rendering props | API calls, Redux, feature business rules |
| **Container** | Input normalization, default config, composing child components | Heavy presentational markup |
| **Utils** | Country config, masks, validators | React hooks or JSX |

## Assets

- Flags, icons, illustrations → `src/assets/` (e.g. `src/assets/flags/in.svg`)
- Reference assets from a config map in `{feature}.utils.ts`, not inline SVG in components
- Adding a country = add asset file + extend `COUNTRY_CONFIG`

## Rules

- One feature per folder (`phone-number/`, not nested under `auth/` unless auth-specific)
- Consumers import from the feature root: `@/components/shared/phone-number`
- Sub-pieces get their own file in `components/` when reused or independently styled
- Use `container/` only when the UI component would otherwise own non-presentational logic
- `src/components/ui/` stays design-system primitives — do not put feature code there

## Example

```tsx
// components/PhoneNumberInput.tsx — UI only
const PhoneNumberInput = ({ value, onChange }) => ( ... );

// container/PhoneNumberInputContainer.tsx — sanitization
const PhoneNumberInputContainer = ({ onChange, ...props }) => (
  <PhoneNumberInput {...props} onChange={(v) => onChange(sanitizePhoneDigits(v))} />
);

// index.ts
export { default as PhoneNumberInput } from "./container/PhoneNumberInputContainer";
```
